@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-Search 1.03

                 ToolTypes for MDB-Search 1.03
                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Actually there no tooltypes, perhaps in feature releases.

@endnode

@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For Z"

                       ToolTypes for Z
                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level
                                  that the user must have to run the door.
                                  Eg. ACCESS=10

LOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door
                                  is located.
                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-Search/MDB-Search
                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!

MULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may
                                  started in different nodes.
                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES

PRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos
                                  priority when the Door is executed.
                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2

STACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.
                                  Eg. STACK=8096

TYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.
                                  This Door is written in 100% pure
                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM

@endnode

@node PART_05 "Commands"

Start the door by useing the Z-command, and will get the main menu.

@{" S "} Toggles between 'All conferences' and 'Current conference'
    to scan.

@{" D "} Toggles between 'All dirs' and 'Upload dirs only' to scan.

@{" Z "} Enter the string you like to find. Okay, its not case sensitive.

@{" G "} Go searching the string.

@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.

@{" Q "} Don't try.

@endnode

@node PART_06 "Changes"

1.03 (12-Jun-1994)
    - Coding enhanced.
    - Search routine improved. Previous versions had a little bug, if 
      you're looking for the string "abc" and somewhere in the dir
      was stated "aabc", the string wasn't found. Shame on me for
      not testing this nasty string.

1.2 (02-Jun-1994)
    - If Exorcist was used in the dir, it doesn't matter anymore.
      The scan will recognise it now!

1.1 (02-Jun-1994)
    - Bug fixed: last file entry in a dir wasn't scanned!

1.0 (29-May-1994)
    - First release.

@endnode

